&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;Could you&amp;#8230; Could you&amp;#8230;&amp;quot; Her body tries to hold back what it&#039;s about to say, then relaxes. &amp;quot;&amp;#8230;Could you kill me?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#039;s fine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Heavy moments slip past. The air is vacuous and heatless. Metallic gears, far out of her body&#039;s vision, whirr while a ghostly machine constructs itself behind her. The pillow falls from her grip, her whole body relaxing. The world is gray.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;Hey, Stacey?&amp;quot; Gunhead says in a whisper.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world is gray, soon to be colorless.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;One of my trilobite hunting pals told me a thing once, when we were patrolling at night through clouds of glowing bacteria.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world is gray, soon to be colorless; that is just fine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;It was that good people make bad liars.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That is just fine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;They are right.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world around SCP-3009-C shatters.&lt;/p&gt;
